---
/**
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SEEING.MD HOME PAGE
 * Route: /
 * Type: Page
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * PURPOSE
 * Introduces SEEING.md as a portable perception specification for people and
 * AI. Shows how unseen human assumptions can become decisions, systems, and
 * actions at scale, then gives visitors a direct way to use and help refine it.
 *
 * AUDIENCE AND PRIMARY ACTION
 * - Audience: Leaders, teams, AI practitioners, designers, developers,
 *   consultants, coaches, and individual practitioners
 * - Primary action: Choose a clear path through the Start Here modal
 * - Supporting action: Download SEEING.md and begin using it immediately
 * - Leader action: Request a private 30-minute Seeing First session, alone or
 *   with a team
 *
 * EXPERIENCE / STRUCTURE
 * 1. Establish that AI scales what people see and what they do not see.
 * 2. Identify perception as the missing layer beneath human intent.
 * 3. Explain the three operating behaviors: separate, surface, and ask.
 * 4. Present Seeing First as a private experience for leaders and teams.
 * 5. Place SEEING.md accurately within the larger field of AI safety.
 * 6. Provide the project instruction and direct download.
 * 7. Close with the work's origin in The Perception Miracle and its influence
 *    from Brian Gardner's exploration of DESIGN.md.
 *
 * KEY RESPONSIBILITIES
 * - Serve the canonical specification from /SEEING.md.
 * - Give first-time visitors three plain-language ways to begin.
 * - Connect leaders to the Seeing First session through Cal.com.
 * - Connect the file to the deeper work at SEE DIFFERENT without obscuring the
 *   primary download action.
 *
 * DEPENDENCIES
 * - Layout: Standalone Astro page; no shared layout dependency
 * - Assets: /favicon.svg and the generated public copy of /SEEING.md
 * - Services: Google Fonts, Cal.com, and SEE DIFFERENT
 * - Hosting: Cloudflare Workers with Static Assets
 *
 * EDITING GUARDRAILS
 * - Preserve the Suede-inspired typography, spacing, black-and-white palette,
 *   and restrained use of #aa6600.
 * - Keep the downloadable specification synchronized with the canonical
 *   SEEING.md file at the repository root.
 * - Keep the Seeing First pathway distinct from downloading SEEING.md.
 * - Keep Start Here choices outcome-based and free of technical language.
 * - Do not imply that SEEING.md resolves every category of AI safety risk.
 * - Keep the book as the primary source and the DESIGN.md influence in the
 *   closing origin section rather than the opening argument.
 * - Keep external links secure with rel="noopener".
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

const title = 'SEEING.md — The Perception Layer for AI';
const description =
  'An open perception specification that helps people and AI surface consequential assumptions before they become decisions at scale.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#11110f" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://seeing.md/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://seeing.md/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Google+Sans+Flex:opsz,wdth,wght@6..144,75..125,100..1000&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="SEEING.md home">SEEING<span>.md</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="#why">Why</a>
        <a href="#seeing-first">Seeing First</a>
        <a href="#use">Use it</a>
        <button class="nav-start start-trigger" type="button">Start Here</button>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">An open perception specification</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">AI scales what we see.<br />And what we don’t.</h1>
          <p class="hero-deck">
            SEEING.md helps people and AI surface consequential assumptions before
            they become decisions, systems, and actions at scale.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <button class="button button-primary start-trigger" type="button">Start Here</button>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/SEEING.md" download>Download SEEING.md</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sequence" aria-label="Seeing leads to intent, system, and scale">
          <span>Seeing</span>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Intent</span>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>System</span>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Scale</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="statement" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-number">01 / The missing layer</p>
          <h2 id="why-title">
            We are trying to align AI with human intent without examining what
            shaped the intent.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="statement-body">
          <p>
            Before a system is designed, trained, evaluated, prompted, or
            deployed, people have already decided what matters, what the problem
            is, what should be measured, and what a good outcome looks like.
          </p>
          <p>
            Most of those decisions do not feel like decisions. They feel like
            reality. SEEING.md introduces a pause before that invisible choice
            becomes machine-scale action.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="outcome-list">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Separate</h3>
            <p>Distinguish what is known from what has already been interpreted.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Surface</h3>
            <p>Make consequential assumptions visible before they become direction.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Ask</h3>
            <p>Pause for one clear question when missing meaning could change the action.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="narrative" id="seeing-first" aria-labelledby="seeing-first-title">
        <div class="narrative-copy">
          <p class="section-number">02 / For leaders · Seeing First</p>
          <h2 id="seeing-first-title">See what shapes thousands of decisions before they are made.</h2>
          <p>
            One human assumption can now shape thousands of decisions. The
            question is no longer only whether a decision is sound, but what
            perception is making it seem necessary. Seeing First helps leaders
            notice what is shaping the decision, loosen what already appears
            certain, and make room to see what the present actually requires.
          </p>
          <div class="offer-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="https://cal.com/billfox/seeing-first" rel="noopener">Experience Seeing First <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <span class="offer-meta">30 minutes · Leader or team</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="signal-map" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="source-node"></span>
          <span class="signal-trunk"></span>
          <span class="signal-spine"></span>
          <div class="signal-branches">
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="scope" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-number">03 / Its place in AI safety</p>
          <h2 id="scope-title">Upstream, not all-encompassing.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>What it addresses</h3>
            <p>
              The human assumptions that enter a system through its purpose,
              data, measures, prompts, evaluation, and use—and can become more
              consequential as the system scales.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>What it does not</h3>
            <p>
              It does not prevent autonomous behavior, malicious use,
              cyberattacks, deception, or loss of control. Those risks require
              technical, organizational, and public safeguards of their own.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="use" id="use" aria-labelledby="use-title">
        <p class="section-number">04 / Begin</p>
        <h2 id="use-title">One file. One question further upstream.</h2>
        <p class="use-intro">
          Place SEEING.md in a project. Name it in the instructions your AI
          system reads. Apply it when judgment, people, strategy,
          interpretation, or consequential decisions are involved.
        </p>

        <div class="instruction">
          <p class="case-label">Suggested project instruction</p>
          <p>
            Before work involving judgment, people, strategy, interpretation,
            or consequential decisions, read SEEING.md. Use it to examine the
            framing and surface relevant assumptions before acting. Apply it
            proportionally; do not slow straightforward technical work
            unnecessarily.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/SEEING.md" download>Download version 0.1.0</a>
          <button class="text-link start-trigger" type="button">Not sure where to begin? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
        </div>

        <aside class="origin" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
          <p class="section-number">Origin</p>
          <div>
            <h2 id="origin-title">The file is open. The practice is relational.</h2>
            <p>
              SEEING.md emerged primarily from Bill Fox’s book,
              <em>The Perception Miracle</em>, and more than 500 explorations into
              how the mind’s past enters the present. The Perception Space is where
              that inquiry becomes an ongoing human practice through images,
              stillness, inquiry, and conversation.
            </p>
            <p>
              Its form was influenced by Brian Gardner’s exploration of DESIGN.md
              as a way to make the intent behind a design system legible to AI.
              SEEING.md carries the inquiry one level further upstream.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link dark-link" href="https://seedifferent.xyz" rel="noopener">Explore SEE DIFFERENT <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </section>
    </main>

    <dialog class="start-modal" id="start-here" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div class="modal-panel">
        <button class="modal-close" type="button" aria-label="Close Start Here">Close</button>
        <p class="section-number">Start here</p>
        <h2 id="start-title">What would be most useful now?</h2>
        <div class="start-options">
          <a href="/SEEING.md" download>
            <span class="option-number">01</span>
            <span>
              <strong>Use SEEING.md</strong>
              <small>Download the file and add it to an AI project.</small>
            </span>
            <i aria-hidden="true">↓</i>
          </a>
          <a href="#why" data-close-modal>
            <span class="option-number">02</span>
            <span>
              <strong>Understand the idea</strong>
              <small>See why perception comes before intent.</small>
            </span>
            <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
          </a>
          <a href="https://cal.com/billfox/seeing-first" rel="noopener">
            <span class="option-number">03</span>
            <span>
              <strong>Bring a real decision</strong>
              <small>Experience Seeing First in 30 minutes.</small>
            </span>
            <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </dialog>

    <footer>
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">SEEING<span>.md</span></a>
      <p>Seeing is the first decision.</p>
      <a href="mailto:hello@seeing.md">hello@seeing.md</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --ink: #000000;
    --paper: #ffffff;
    --muted: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    --line-dark: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    --line-light: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
    --amber: #aa6600;
    --content: 1280px;
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Google Sans Flex", Inter, ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .site-header,
  .hero,
  main > section,
  footer {
    padding-inline: max(24px, calc((100vw - var(--content)) / 2));
  }

  .site-header {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 2;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    display: flex;
    width: 100%;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding-block: 30px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .wordmark {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .wordmark span {
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 30px;
  }

  nav a,
  footer a {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  nav a {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .nav-start,
  .text-link,
  .button {
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .nav-start {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--paper);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 100svh;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;
    padding-top: 140px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 960px;
    align-self: center;
    padding-block: 60px 100px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-number,
  .case-label {
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    color: var(--amber);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 5vw, 60px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .hero-deck {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 42px 0 0;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 52px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 13px 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--amber);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 250ms ease-out, color 250ms ease-out, border-color 250ms ease-out;
  }

  .button-primary {
    border-color: var(--amber);
    background: var(--amber);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .button-secondary {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .button:hover,
  .button:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--amber);
    background: var(--amber);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .sequence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 22px;
    padding-top: 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .sequence span:first-child {
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .sequence i {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--amber);
  }

  main > section:not(.hero) {
    padding-block: clamp(80px, 9vw, 100px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .statement {
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .statement h2,
  .section-heading h2,
  .use h2,
  .origin h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4vw, 60px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .statement h2 {
    max-width: 1020px;
  }

  .statement-body {
    margin-left: calc(20% + 60px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .statement-body p,
  .scope-grid p,
  .origin p {
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.35fr) 1.65fr;
    gap: 60px;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
  }

  .outcome-list {
    margin-top: 80px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .outcome-list article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(70px, 0.35fr) 0.65fr 1fr;
    gap: 30px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: 30px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .outcome-list span {
    color: var(--amber);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  .outcome-list h3,
  .scope-grid h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .outcome-list p {
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  }

  .narrative {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  }

  .narrative {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .narrative-copy h2 {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4vw, 60px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .narrative-copy > p:not(.section-number) {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 40px 0 0;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  }

  .offer-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .offer-meta {
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .signal-map {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 360px;
  }

  .source-node {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 8%;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--amber);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }

  .signal-trunk {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 8%;
    width: 34%;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--amber);
  }

  .signal-spine {
    position: absolute;
    top: 15%;
    bottom: 15%;
    left: 42%;
    width: 1px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }

  .signal-branches {
    position: absolute;
    top: 15%;
    right: 8%;
    bottom: 15%;
    left: 42%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .signal-branches i {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }

  .signal-branches i::after {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: 0;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink);
    content: "";
    transform: translate(50%, -50%);
  }

  .scope-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .scope {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .scope .section-heading,
  .scope-grid {
    border-color: var(--line-dark);
  }

  .scope-grid {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
  }

  .scope-grid > div {
    padding: 48px 56px 0 0;
  }

  .scope-grid > div + div {
    padding-left: 56px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
  }

  .scope-grid p {
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .use {
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .use .section-number {
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .use h2 {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .use-intro {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 36px 0 0;
    font-size: 1.18rem;
  }

  .instruction {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin-top: 60px;
    padding: 30px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--amber);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  }

  .instruction .case-label {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .instruction p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: 8px;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    text-underline-offset: 5px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .text-link span {
    margin-left: 8px;
  }

  .origin {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.35fr) 1.65fr;
    gap: 60px;
    margin-top: 100px;
    padding-top: 80px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .origin > div {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .origin p {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .dark-link {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .start-modal {
    width: min(720px, calc(100vw - 32px));
    max-height: calc(100svh - 32px);
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .start-modal::backdrop {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.78);
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  }

  .modal-panel {
    position: relative;
    padding: clamp(32px, 6vw, 64px);
  }

  .modal-panel h2 {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 52px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .modal-close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 24px;
    right: 24px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .start-options {
    margin-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .start-options a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 36px 1fr auto;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 24px;
